            <ArticleTitle>Hyperventilation: An important cause of pseudoangina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>50 patients initially referred to a cardiac clinic for confirmation or exclusion of angina were found to be habitual hyperventilators. 13 of them also had some organic heart disease. Simple physiotherapy aimed at restoring a normal breathing pattern proved an effective treatment, 76% of those followed for 11-68 months being symptom-free.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
